    mark "Hmmmm. So this is fabric from the future, huh...? Strange stuff."

    narrator "It was something I couldn't quite put my finger on. It looked like someone had meshed together sea foam, cotton candy and snow together and flattened them into a fabric."

    narrator "Even if I didn't believe it was from 240 years in the future, it was certainly interesting."

    mark "It's nice. And you're right, it is pretty soft."

    julie "Hehe. That makes me happy."

    mark "Well, if you say so."

