    narrator "The sky was blue, but the sun wasn't glaring too brightly so you didn't quite have to squint looking up."

    julie "Papa would really like to see this. The clouds don't look like this in the future. They're dark and dirty-looking, and... well..."

    mark "Too bad for him that he's not with you. Why don't you bring him along with you, some time?"

    julie "........."


    # --------------------------------------------------------------
    # Julie's Father
    # --------------------------------------------------------------

    hide julie

    scene cg julie_explains at old_cg

    julie "If I could, I would. But you know... Papa's an invalid."

    mark "Oh? That right?"

    julie "Mmmm. If he gave up his research and his time machine, he'd probably just be left alone."

    julie "But he keeps tampering with things that shouldn't be tampered with--or so they say--and people always seem to be after him."

    mark "Really? You seem to be doing pretty well."

    julie "Hehe. They can't get ahold of me even if they try. I'm too sneaky."


    # Return to the field.

    scene bg dandelion_field at old_bg

    mark "Mmmm, makes me wonder if that's something to be proud of..."

    show julie happy at center

    narrator "Julie and I both laughed together."

    narrator "I wasn't entirely sure what to make of it--the 'my father is an invalid' part--so I just left it alone."

    narrator "Maybe it was something better off unknown."

    show julie curious at center

    julie "Hmhmhmhmhm. Well, it was really fun Mr. Mark, but I should be going."

    mark "Oh yeah? Going back to the future?"

    show julie relaxed at center

    julie "Hehe. For now. Papa needs his supper, and I have to clean my bedroom."

    show julie giggle at center

    julie "It's kind of messy."

    mark "Sounds important. Will I see you again?"

